<statement>
<p>What are the solutions to <m>\displaystyle{4}{x}^{{2}}+{90}{x}+{1}={0}</m>? <fillin characters="12"/></p>
<p>Round results to 2 decimal places.</p>

</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>-0.01,-22.49</li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p><m>\displaystyle{x}=\frac{{-{\left({90}\right)}\pm\sqrt{{{\left({90}\right)}^{{2}}-{4}{\left({4}\right)}{\left({1}\right)}}}}}{{{2}{\left({4}\right)}}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}=\frac{{-{90}\pm\sqrt{{{8100}-{\left({16}\right)}}}}}{{8}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}=\frac{{-{90}\pm\sqrt{{{8084}}}}}{{8}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}=\frac{{-{90}\pm{89.911067171956}}}{{8}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}=-{0.011116603505489},-{22.488883396495}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}=-{0.01},-{22.49}</m></p>
</solution>
